WEBVTT

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.200
- Who are you?
- I stole a car. Crashed it.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.900
Then my mom threw me out.
So Mr. Cohen took me in.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.500
- You brought him home?
- What do you guys do around here?

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.600
- What do you think of Newport?
- I can get in less trouble where I'm from.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.300
- You have no idea.
- Shouldn't her boyfriend do this?

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.700
Sure they're not doing anything
we didn't do.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.600
- My dad's not here.
- It's just a thing with a client.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.100
- Put him down.
- Hey, Ryan.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.300
- Welcome to the O.C., bitch.
- I don't want this kid in my house.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.100
Guys, come on. Out of the pool.
Dinner's almost ready.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Dad, I know.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.700
I understand how important the model
home is to the new development.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.000
We'll sell the lots by Christmas,
I promise.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.200
Okay. Bye.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.300
I wish there was more we could do.
Honey, you're his lawyer,
not his guardian.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.200
I know. In the morning
I'll take him to Child Services.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:31.000
What kind of mother
just abandons her child?

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.800
- What happens if they don't find her?
- He'll go into the system.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.000
Foster care till he's 18.
I mean, they'll try and place him...

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.500
...but at his age it'll be impossible.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.500
You know what I was thinking?

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:01.900
This being your last night and all,
we should do something special.
I don't know what.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.800
Possibly get a couple of tattoos or some
hookers and lose our virginity, right?

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.000
Okay, dude, there's a shark movie
at the IMAX if that's what you're into.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.700
I think I just want to take it easy.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.200
How was your swim?

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.100
It was great.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.100
What's that?

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.100
It's a model home.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.900
I build them.
Well, the real ones, not that one.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.000
Can you build me one?

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.200
Sorry. Bad joke.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.100
Thanks.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.500
So...

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.700
...the last supper, huh?

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.900
Sorry. Bad joke.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:05.600
It's just a laugh riot around here.
- This all looks really good.
- Too bad you're leaving.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:11.000
- We never eat like this.
- That's not true. I cook all the time.
Dad.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.800
I'm sorry, honey.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.300
Let's just eat.
We're not saying
we want you to cook more.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:22.300
- Remember the meat loaf incident of '98?
- That was brisket.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.600
Yeah, that's my point exactly.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.700
As your attorney, I'll cosign these forms.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:37.700
They basically say that you don't have
a legal parent or a guardian available.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.700
So I'm now property of the
government, nickname 0382965.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.000
Hey, it's better than "Death Breath Seth."

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.100
Or so I would imagine.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.600
So we'll meet with your social worker
in the morning...

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.400
...and she'll be the one
to take you to the group home.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.300
My contact at Child Services got you in
with only two other kids, which is good.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.100
- It can get crowded.
- Thanks. I appreciate it.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.800
And, you know...

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.400
...they do find foster homes
for kids your age.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.000
Yeah, because everybody wants
a brand-new teenager.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.700
I'm sorry if I'm the only one
that'll state the obvious...

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.400
...but we have all this extra room.
We have a pool house.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:23.100
Yet you guys are gonna ship him off
to a group home? Am I the only one...

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:27.000
...who gets how much that sucks?
- It's okay. Really.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.500
Good luck with it. It looks perfect.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.500
- Good night.
- Good night.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.200
Hey, how about a little...

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.400
...PlayStation perhaps?

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:11.000
- Are you running away?
- Go back in the house, Seth.
Hey, you can't just run away.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.000
What are you thinking?
What about Child Services or my dad?

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:20.600
Okay, then wait.
I want to come with you.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:24.200
Know what I've always wanted to do,
besides sail to Tahiti? That Kerouac thing.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:28.900
Hit the road, stop at diner to diner,
the pancake tour of North America.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:30.900
- No.
- Fair enough.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.800
- Where you going?
- I don't know.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:38.200
New town, get a job, save some money.
Great plan.
You've given it a lot of thought.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.300
Got a better idea?

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.100
Actually, I do.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.300
Seth?

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.400
Can I talk to you?

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.600
Dad?

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:15.800
- What, is it morning?
- You're asleep?

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.200
Yeah, I was. What's going on?

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.400
Well...

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:25.600
...I wanted to talk about Ryan.
Yeah, I know. It's cool.
We don't need to discuss it.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:30.000
I think we do. I know you're upset,
your mother and I are upset.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.800
But our responsibility is to our family.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.900
It's okay. I get it.
This is a person's life we're talking about.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.500
We need to leave it
in the hands of the authorities.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:41.400
- There's no need for sarcasm.
- I'm not being sarcastic.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:46.500
Well, it's hard to tell sometimes.
Dad?

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:49.100
It's okay. Really.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:54.200
- When you want to talk about it...
- I know. You're the one to talk to. Got it.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.900
Good night.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:00.300
- Good night.
- Night.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.200
Come on, Seth.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.500
Okay, got it. I'll be there in,
like, 20 minutes.

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:30.900
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.300
I didn't think I'd see you again.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:39.000
Look, I wanted to say thanks
for the other night.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.600
You always drink like that?

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.800
- I thought you left.
- I did. I am.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:52.600
Ryan. Ryan, I'm all set. Ready?

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.500
Hi there, Marissa.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:58.400
- What are you doing?
- Nothing. We're just hanging out.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:01.700
Look, it's somebody's birthday.
My invitation got lost in the mail.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:06.500
It's my friend Summer's birthday.
Summer's birthday is not till Wednesday.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:12.100
That's what I heard.
I don't know. I guessed.
You guys are up to something.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.400
- Dude, what did you tell her?
- I didn't tell her anything.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:19.500
Maybe the black turtleneck in August
tipped her off.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.700
Okay, I was going for stealth.
Also, it's slimming.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.500
We should really go.
Have fun at your party.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:30.600
You should probably be off.
The Newport social scene awaits.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.700
Oh, yeah?

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:39.400
Why won't you tell me where we're
going? This is pretty far away.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:44.200
Oh, wow, complaining. That's interesting,
considering nobody invited you.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:47.800
Before I came along
you were on a skateboard.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:56.200
- You like them?
- Yeah, I guess.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:59.700
- Well, what do you like?
- Everything.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.300
I don't know,
I don't really listen to music.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:08.500
- Dude, that's kind of weird.
- Why? What do you like?
Right now, punk.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:10.900
Avril Lavigne doesn't count as punk.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:16.100
What about the Cramps?
Stiff Little Fingers. The Clash. Sex Pistols.

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:20.100
I listen to the same music
as Marissa Cooper?

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:25.300
- I think I have to kill myself.
- You listen to punk, huh?
I'm angry.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.900
That's it right there.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:37.400
- Looks scary.
- Then you can stay in the car.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.700
Do you recognize this place, Ryan?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.400
- This isn't...
- Where are we?

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:48.000
Well, it's one of my mom's
housing developments.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.200
Her and my grandpa own a bunch
of them. This is supposed to be...

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.700
...the model home,
but it never got finished.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:59.700
Why? Did someone die here
and now it's haunted?
Yes. That's exactly what happened.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.800
- What did happen?
- I don't know.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.800
How do contractors just disappear?

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:09.700
If we don't have a model home,
we don't have a new development.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:14.000
It's been a month.
I'm not waiting for you guys anymore.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:21.100
- You know where to reach me.
- No luck with the contractors?
Vanished.

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:25.000
My father's never gonna
let me hear the end of this.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:28.200
Did you...? Did you talk to Seth?

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.100
I think so. Don't blame yourself.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:37.200
I'm not blaming myself. But how can I
allow a strange boy to live in this house?

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:40.800
Seth needs to know
it's what any mother would do.

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:44.100
I was talking about the contractors.

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.500
So you want him to stay here?

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.700
Well, I mean, I know the place
needs some sprucing up, but...

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.800
God, did I just say "sprucing"?

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.400
So, Ryan, what do you think?

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:04.900
I haven't really had time to think.
But how much better is this place
than some group home?

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.800
And wait till you see the best part.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.300
- It's an empty pool.
- To some people.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:26.700
So your mom... I mean,
she has to come back, right?

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:31.300
I don't know.
My mom's kind of a train wreck.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.400
So's mine.

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:41.300
What about your dad?
Can you call him?

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.700
Dad's in jail. Armed robbery.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.800
Impressive, huh?

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:57.500
My dad, he's, like, a financial planner.
And I think he's in trouble.

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.800
I don't have any stock tips.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:08.900
He stopped going to the office.
And these guys keep showing up
at the door, like cops.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:11.400
But he won't answer.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:17.800
- Look, I haven't told anybody that.
- I can keep a secret.

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:27.200
- Hey.
- Where you at, girl?

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:30.300
It's time for you to get your buzz on.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:35.200
Nordlund is so faded
he can't even feel his feet.
There goes the left leg!

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:39.700
I miss you, babe. You know
it's not a party without you.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:42.100
- Oh, you're sweet.
- What's the deal?

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:46.200
You were supposed to be here
an hour ago.
Okay, I'll be there soon.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.500
Say hi to everyone.

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:51.200
All right. Love you.

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.600
Love you too.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.700
Bye.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:10.200
So how long you been with him?

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:11.900
Luke?

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:14.900
- I don't know, really.
- I know.

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:17.100
Fifth grade, when you two
got your mack on...

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.800
...during our class trip to the
Museum of Tolerance, back of the bus.
Classy lady.

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:24.600
You know what?
What's your problem, Cohen?

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.200
- I mean, what did I ever do to you?
- Nothing.

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:31.200
I've lived next door to you forever, and
you've never done or said anything to me.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.300
Oh, my God. You're the one
who never talks to me.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:38.500
You think you're so much better
than everyone.
I do?

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:43.400
Well, if you're talking about Luke,
then, yes...

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:46.200
...because that guy shaves his chest!

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:51.800
He plays water polo.
We know. Half the team
tried to kill us the other night.

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:56.700
I'm not too popular around here.
And your boyfriend...

00:14:56.900 --> 00:15:02.100
...a little bit angry.
- You didn't try to hit him back?
- Actually, I hit him first.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.600
Well, hard to believe
you're not more popular.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.300
I thought this could be your room.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:18.200
I still don't know if it's a good idea
for me to stick around.
You should stay.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:24.800
- Okay. For a little while.
- So when she says it, you listen?

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.600
- Hey, Summer.
- Hey, is that Summer?

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:34.400
- Tell her I said happy birthday.
- Okay.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:39.300
Coop, where are you?
We're coming to get you.
Oh, no, don't. I'm coming.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:43.700
- Tell her I said happy birthday.
- Seth Cohen says happy birthday.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.500
- Who?
- She says thanks.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.900
Look, I gotta go. Okay. Bye.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.400
I gotta go meet my friends.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:57.900
My other friends.

00:15:57.900 --> 00:15:59.800
I should get back too
and protect my cover.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:04.100
But wait. Listen. We have to promise
not to tell anyone about this place, okay?

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:10.500
Now, Ryan's not going to, obviously,
and I could get grounded.
So that leaves Marissa.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.900
I can keep a secret.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:16.300
Okay. See you tomorrow.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:19.500
Me too. We'll fix this place up.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.900
- Cool.
- I'm telling you, Ryan...

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:29.000
...this plan is foolproof.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.400
Ryan?

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:51.000
Hey, Ryan? You ready?

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:11.700
Okay, the key here is not to panic.
Do you have your supplies?

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:15.200
Yeah, but there are cops at your house.
Do you think it's safe?

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:20.300
I'll handle Johnny Law, unless...
Are you losing your nerve?
Meet me in the driveway.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:28.000
He couldn't have gotten far.
We'll search the neighborhood.

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:31.900
Seth, I was just gonna get you.
We gotta talk about Ryan.

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:38.300
Marissa, look who's here.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:44.300
- Luke, hi.
- Hey.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:49.000
Just grabbing a little grub
before we take the boat out.
Boat?

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:54.100
I thought we'd take my dad's Donzi.
Do a little waterskiing,
have a little lunch.

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:05.300
So you have no idea
where Ryan might have gone?
I don't know.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.700
He did say something about
going down to Mexico...

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:10.600
...and gambling on cockfights.
I mean, I don't know what...

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:13.200
Quit joking. Answer his question.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:18.300
Yes, I did. I really don't know. I do not
know the guy. I never got the chance.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:23.600
Hey, there's eggs.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.600
Oh, I'm taking Kaitlin to the stables,
so I need that check.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:31.300
Does Kaitlin really need a pony?
In a couple months,
she's not even gonna like horses.

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:34.600
What? I love China.
She's the prettiest pony.

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:39.000
We're not giving up China.
Wait in the car, sweetie.
Mommy will be right with you.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:47.900
Jimmy, all this work
is making you so tense.

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:49.900
Look, I gotta...

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.000
I've gotta talk to you
about work.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:55.000
You know I don't like to talk
about work.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:58.200
Yeah, well, I've made...

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:00.400
...a few mistakes...

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:05.600
...and I don't know really...
Jimmy, you don't have cancer.
No one is dying.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:09.900
Whatever it is, whatever you've done,
I'm sure you'll fix it.

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:14.300
Can you write that check?
I don't want Kaitlin to be late. Okay?

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:18.400
It's just, Suki is amazing. It doesn't
hurt at all when she's waxing you.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:20.300
It's really hard to get an appointment.

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:25.300
Why don't you get a manicure?
You could come with me.
I mean, they're not just for girls.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:27.800
You go. We'll catch up later.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.800
Holly's having a...

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.400
- Holly's having a thing.
- Perfect.

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:45.800
- So did you tell him anything?
- No. But if anyone asks, you're Suki.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:50.200
So you didn't tell them anything?

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:54.400
Actually, I told them you went
to Mexico for cockfights.

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:58.600
You know what,
even if they don't believe me...
...they'll never look for you here.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.300
- Did you seriously bring a loofa?
- What's a loofa?

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:05.500
You said bring whatever
was around the house.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:09.200
But I meant, like, survival supplies,
like rope or muskets...

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:13.800
...and not Kiehl's cucumber moisturizer.

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:22.200
- That's a pretty good call.
- That's nice.

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:32.800
Hey.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:36.900
Here's a little bit of everything.

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.900
Let your education begin.

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:43.900
This place is perfect.
Seriously, it's totally safe.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.000
Ryan, how perfect is this place, right?

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:50.400
- What else could you need?
- Anyone bring any food?

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:54.000
Food. Guess we're going on a mission.

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:15.000
Faster! Come on!

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:43.600
Call me if someone meeting that
description comes in. Thank you.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:48.200
- Nothing at the hospitals.
- I'm sure he'll turn up.
I think Seth knows where he is.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:52.600
Are you accusing him of lying?
That'll be good for your relationship.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:56.700
- Let the police handle this.
- I wish you hadn't called the police.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:01.100
They don't have the resources
or the manpower.
Ryan will slip through the cracks.

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:06.100
Sandy, how many of these cases
have you seen...
...have passed across your desk?

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:13.300
What is it about this kid?

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:16.800
I thought I could help him,
make a difference.

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:19.100
I was this kid.

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:22.400
If someone hadn't helped me...

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:26.100
...I wouldn't be here.

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:33.900
Hello?

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:43.300
- How are you?
- I'm good. I hate to ask, but...

00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:47.200
...I need your help with something.
Of course.

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:52.200
China has alopecia.
We need to call the vet.

00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:59.800
- Are you free for lunch?
- Yeah.

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:04.100
I have some stuff I need to do for work,
but lunch sounds great.

00:23:05.200 --> 00:23:08.300
So, you guys,
I've been thinking about a plan.

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:12.000
You know, right now,
this could very well be...

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:14.700
...the first stop on our pancake tour
of North America.

00:23:14.900 --> 00:23:18.300
Like in On the Road?
That's my favorite book.

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:20.900
Mine too.

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.700
So here's the deal.

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:27.600
My mom had this boyfriend, he hired me
to work construction last summer.

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:32.300
But then they broke up.
He moved away to Austin.

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:34.400
In Texas.

00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:38.500
- He said if I was ever there, look him up.
- Well, I mean...

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:42.300
That's kind of far. We were thinking, like,
Long Beach, so we could still hang out.

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:45.400
I'll need to get a couple days of work
so I can get travel money.

00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:48.300
Well, I mean, we can get you money.

00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:55.500
Well, I mean, you know,
I guess in a way you're lucky.

00:23:55.900 --> 00:23:59.700
You get to move to a new place,
start over, be whoever you want to be.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.400
That's really not so bad.

00:24:08.700 --> 00:24:09.900
Hey.

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:13.700
- What's it take to get a menu?
- I'll handle it.

00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:16.000
- No, I'll handle it.
- And ruin your popularity?

00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:19.900
You know what, why don't you guys
just sneak out the back.

00:24:22.300 --> 00:24:24.500
What's going on with you two?

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:27.000
Hey, how's it going?

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:32.000
Oh, it was great. It was really good.

00:24:34.100 --> 00:24:36.700
Hey! Front door.

00:24:41.400 --> 00:24:44.700
- I was thinking we could go to Holly's.
- Thanks.

00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:46.800
- Sounds good.
- Awesome.

00:24:46.900 --> 00:24:49.200
So, what did you guys do today?

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:58.500
Hi. How you doing? You like
the food here too? It's pretty awesome.
Shut up, queer.

00:24:59.400 --> 00:25:03.400
Well, at least I don't shave my chest.
- What did you say?
- Luke, come on.

00:25:03.700 --> 00:25:06.400
I said, you look nice in a sweater vest.
It was a compliment.

00:25:06.600 --> 00:25:09.700
- Do you want me to break you, Cohen?
- Hi.

00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:13.600
No way. Look who's back.

00:25:13.900 --> 00:25:17.600
- You're a little far from 8 Mile.
- Luke, don't.

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:21.000
What are you, like, spokesperson
for Geeks of America or something?

00:25:21.700 --> 00:25:24.300
You know what I like about rich kids?

00:25:25.600 --> 00:25:26.800
Nothing.

00:25:27.600 --> 00:25:31.900
- That was awesome!
- Come here, you punk!
Come on, man! Come here!

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:37.600
Cohen, you're dead meat, man!
You're dead meat!

00:25:37.900 --> 00:25:39.300
Go!

00:25:40.600 --> 00:25:43.100
Come on, chump! You're dead!

00:25:51.400 --> 00:25:54.100
"You know what I like about rich kids?

00:25:54.400 --> 00:25:55.600
Nothing. " Hey, Ryan...

00:25:55.900 --> 00:26:00.500
...you wouldn't consider me rich, would
you? I'd be more upper-middle class.

00:26:02.900 --> 00:26:04.500
What's up, fool?

00:26:05.200 --> 00:26:09.800
- You know, you didn't have to hit him.
- Sorry.
You know, the cashier called the cops.

00:26:13.700 --> 00:26:16.600
Look, I don't know why
Luke does that.

00:26:16.900 --> 00:26:19.400
- Did that. He's just...
- An ass?

00:26:19.900 --> 00:26:21.700
Protective.

00:26:29.600 --> 00:26:31.500
God, it's my mom.

00:26:35.100 --> 00:26:37.500
And your dad.

00:26:40.600 --> 00:26:42.400
It's been a while.

00:26:42.700 --> 00:26:46.500
I have to figure out
what kind of shape this place is in.

00:26:53.200 --> 00:26:57.000
That's what those contractors
have been doing.

00:26:58.900 --> 00:27:01.300
This place is fantastic.

00:27:01.600 --> 00:27:03.700
- You don't think it's too much?
- Are you kidding?

00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:06.300
You're talking to a guy
whose wife just imported...

00:27:06.600 --> 00:27:09.900
...ceramic shower-curtain rings
from Morocco.

00:27:13.500 --> 00:27:17.300
This is gorgeous,
with the high ceilings and the molding.

00:27:17.700 --> 00:27:19.800
It reminds me of...

00:27:20.100 --> 00:27:22.100
- Your parents' house.
- On Elm Grove.

00:27:22.300 --> 00:27:27.200
With the vaulted ceilings and those
great beams. Remember that?

00:27:27.600 --> 00:27:29.800
Yeah. I loved that old house.

00:27:29.900 --> 00:27:33.700
Yeah, I loved that place too.
I had my first kiss there.

00:27:33.900 --> 00:27:35.600
Me too.

00:27:37.300 --> 00:27:39.800
So, what's going on, Jimmy?

00:27:44.200 --> 00:27:47.400
I had a really bad year
with the market and...

00:27:47.700 --> 00:27:51.600
Well, it was disastrous. It's gonna
be a struggle just to remain solvent...

00:27:51.900 --> 00:27:54.000
How much do you need?

00:27:56.700 --> 00:28:00.300
It's... It's a lot of money.
It's too much.

00:28:00.600 --> 00:28:02.500
Jimmy.

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:07.700
- It's $100,000.
- I'll call the bank.

00:28:08.400 --> 00:28:10.300
- No, I can't.
- I can.

00:28:11.100 --> 00:28:13.100
I'll pay you back.

00:28:16.500 --> 00:28:20.700
But it's gonna take me
a couple of months.
I know where you live.

00:28:24.600 --> 00:28:26.900
This place is gonna be perfect.

00:28:27.400 --> 00:28:31.900
I hope so. The new contractors come
tomorrow. Better get the job finished.

00:28:31.900 --> 00:28:35.300
New contractors.
Sounds like a nightmare.

00:28:35.600 --> 00:28:37.500
Pretty much.

00:28:39.200 --> 00:28:41.000
Are you okay?

00:28:48.300 --> 00:28:51.000
So the contractors start tomorrow.

00:28:51.600 --> 00:28:53.900
Guess that means I'm gone.

00:28:55.900 --> 00:29:00.000
One bus ticket to Austin,
8 a.m. Tomorrow.

00:29:01.700 --> 00:29:03.900
"Would you like to purchase?"

00:29:10.200 --> 00:29:13.500
- Hey.
- Hey. We're not knocking anymore?

00:29:13.900 --> 00:29:17.400
I'm sorry. What are you doing?
Just busy.

00:29:18.100 --> 00:29:23.600
- You're always busy.
- It's the price of fame. I gotta go, Dad.
They found Ryan.

00:29:25.400 --> 00:29:30.400
Or spotted someone with his description.
There was a fight by the pier.
Really?

00:29:30.600 --> 00:29:32.600
Which means he's probably
still in the area.

00:29:32.900 --> 00:29:36.300
We should find him before the authorities
do. Before he gets in more trouble.

00:29:36.700 --> 00:29:41.800
Actually, do you need me to go?
I was going somewhere.
Seth, he's your friend.

00:29:43.600 --> 00:29:45.100
Yeah, okay.

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:55.000
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:29:55.200 --> 00:29:59.700
So, what's up?
You've been all weird-acting lately.
Yeah?

00:29:59.900 --> 00:30:02.000
I don't know, I guess...

00:30:02.300 --> 00:30:06.000
Do you ever wonder what your life
looks like through someone else's eyes?

00:30:06.400 --> 00:30:11.700
This is what I'm talking about.
What is up with you?
Nothing. It's just...

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:16.900
- Fresh margs!
- This is some weak margarita.
Whatever. You're the lightweight.

00:30:17.700 --> 00:30:20.800
- Say it over here.
- I hope your parents never come home.

00:30:21.100 --> 00:30:25.400
Let's find that punk's trailer park
and burn it to the ground.
Who that?

00:30:25.700 --> 00:30:27.400
That freak from Chino
was up in Luke's grill.

00:30:27.600 --> 00:30:30.700
Maybe he's on OxyContin.
OxyContin is gnarly.

00:30:31.100 --> 00:30:32.700
I heard he's a total psycho.

00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:36.000
He's a little bitch. If I see him again,
I'm gonna beat his ass.

00:30:36.300 --> 00:30:39.500
- Run him out of Newport for sure.
- I gotta go.

00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:47.700
- Hey, wait up. Where you going?
- I can't be here right now.

00:30:48.400 --> 00:30:52.000
- What's the matter?
- You don't know him.
You don't know anything about him.

00:30:58.800 --> 00:31:01.000
- He could be anywhere.
- Dad, I'm sure Ryan's fine.

00:31:01.300 --> 00:31:03.700
We should try again when it's light out.

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:08.100
- It could be too late by then.
- Maybe he's better off on his own.

00:31:08.300 --> 00:31:10.100
What does that mean?

00:31:12.200 --> 00:31:14.800
Okay, if we find him, then what?

00:31:15.200 --> 00:31:19.700
Then, if he's lucky, he gets to go back
with his mom? I would run away too.

00:31:20.900 --> 00:31:25.800
Promise me that you'd never run away,
no matter how bad things may seem.

00:31:26.200 --> 00:31:30.200
- Your mother and I will always be there.
- Take it down a notch.

00:31:30.300 --> 00:31:32.800
The minute you were born I knew...

00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:37.300
...that I would never breathe easy again
without knowing you were safe.

00:31:37.300 --> 00:31:39.000
So I'm like asthma?

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:42.700
I'm warning you, you run away,
I'm coming with you.

00:31:45.900 --> 00:31:48.100
I guess we can keep looking.

00:32:10.100 --> 00:32:12.400
This song reminds me of you.

00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:17.800
- I thought you were with Luke.
- I was.

00:32:20.800 --> 00:32:24.200
I don't know why I'm here.
I just wanted to see you.

00:32:26.400 --> 00:32:30.400
I mean, you're leaving tomorrow,
and what if I never...?

00:32:30.700 --> 00:32:32.400
We never...?

00:32:37.200 --> 00:32:41.300
Maybe I could spend the night...
...just hang out.

00:32:47.500 --> 00:32:49.500
You can't stay.

00:32:50.500 --> 00:32:53.900
If you stay, if we spend the night...

00:32:54.200 --> 00:32:56.400
- I don't know that I could leave.
- Then don't.

00:32:56.700 --> 00:33:01.400
You'll go back to school in the fall,
and I'll just what? Hang around here?

00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:04.500
Hiding like some ghost?

00:33:04.800 --> 00:33:07.900
The cops find me
and I have to disappear again?

00:33:13.900 --> 00:33:16.100
We're from different worlds.

00:33:17.600 --> 00:33:19.200
That's not true.

00:33:20.100 --> 00:33:22.000
I'm not like you.

00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:26.600
Go.

00:33:26.900 --> 00:33:28.500
Please.

00:33:29.000 --> 00:33:30.300
Go.

00:34:07.900 --> 00:34:10.000
Hey, Allen.

00:34:10.300 --> 00:34:15.300
I'm good. I know it's late,
but I need to transfer some money.

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:19.100
Sure, I can hold on a sec.

00:34:47.300 --> 00:34:49.300
Seth, I'm up here.

00:34:50.400 --> 00:34:52.600
You get the bus ticket?

00:34:52.800 --> 00:34:54.600
Bus ticket?

00:34:56.700 --> 00:34:59.100
You're not going anywhere.

00:35:01.100 --> 00:35:03.500
What are you doing here, man?

00:35:03.800 --> 00:35:06.500
What are you doing with my girlfriend?

00:35:06.800 --> 00:35:08.400
Nothing.

00:35:08.700 --> 00:35:10.900
It didn't look like nothing.

00:35:11.700 --> 00:35:13.400
Tell me...

00:35:13.700 --> 00:35:17.600
...or I'll kill you.
- Then kill me and quit talking about it.

00:35:42.800 --> 00:35:46.000
The place is on fire, man.
We gotta go.

00:35:56.100 --> 00:35:57.700
Come on!

00:36:20.100 --> 00:36:21.900
Let's go, man!

00:36:22.200 --> 00:36:23.900
Run.

00:36:40.300 --> 00:36:46.000
I thought basketball season was over.
This is ESPN Classic.
They play all old games.

00:36:46.400 --> 00:36:49.100
So the Lakers-Pistons. Right?

00:36:49.400 --> 00:36:53.800
1986, the finals, game seven.
You remember watching this?

00:36:54.200 --> 00:36:57.400
You were pregnant with Marissa
when this was on.

00:36:57.400 --> 00:36:59.600
I remember. I was so swollen.

00:36:59.900 --> 00:37:01.800
I hated Detroit.

00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:04.400
- Isiah, Laimbeer.
- Yeah.

00:37:04.700 --> 00:37:06.500
Dumars. Oh, my...

00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:10.700
But Worthy, James Worthy,
he saved us. He shot the lights out.

00:37:11.300 --> 00:37:12.700
So fantastic.

00:37:14.500 --> 00:37:16.800
You know that thing I was trying
to talk to you about?

00:37:17.100 --> 00:37:20.900
- Jimmy.
- No, I'm just saying that I took care of it.

00:37:22.800 --> 00:37:25.600
- I knew you would.
- You did?

00:37:28.400 --> 00:37:33.000
I can't believe I'm old enough to have
watched people play in those shorts.

00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:37.700
Hey, Marissa.

00:37:38.500 --> 00:37:39.800
Marissa?

00:37:44.100 --> 00:37:45.800
I'll go.

00:37:46.100 --> 00:37:47.700
Here you go.

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:55.600
Hey.

00:37:57.100 --> 00:37:59.100
What's the matter?

00:38:00.800 --> 00:38:03.400
What's the matter? Come on.

00:38:03.700 --> 00:38:06.000
You can tell me.

00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:10.800
Come here. Give me a hug.
Give me a hug.

00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:13.700
What's the matter?

00:38:15.600 --> 00:38:19.300
You can tell me.
We tell each other everything.

00:38:21.600 --> 00:38:23.000
Do we?

00:38:32.500 --> 00:38:33.900
Hello?

00:38:36.900 --> 00:38:38.900
I'll meet you there.

00:38:48.600 --> 00:38:51.100
- Hi.
- Did Marissa come back?

00:38:51.400 --> 00:38:53.500
You smell like smoke.

00:38:55.000 --> 00:38:57.600
Yeah, we hot-boxed in Nordlund's car.

00:38:57.600 --> 00:39:00.200
And didn't invite me?

00:39:03.300 --> 00:39:05.900
Dude, that kid was messed up.

00:39:06.600 --> 00:39:09.300
- He was breathing.
- I hope so.

00:39:17.900 --> 00:39:20.800
I can't believe this.
This house is cursed.

00:39:22.100 --> 00:39:24.400
- You the owner?
- Yes, I am. What happened?

00:39:24.700 --> 00:39:29.100
Not sure yet. But it looks like
somebody's been living here.
What?

00:39:30.300 --> 00:39:31.900
It's my fault.

00:40:05.600 --> 00:40:08.300
- You're okay.
- Disappointed?

00:40:09.400 --> 00:40:11.400
Where you going?

00:40:12.300 --> 00:40:14.200
Don't know.

00:40:14.400 --> 00:40:18.600
We both keep our mouths shut,
they may never know it was us.

00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:31.200
- What are you doing?
- You're giving me a ride.

00:40:31.500 --> 00:40:34.300
I don't know what happened.
I don't know why it burned down.

00:40:34.600 --> 00:40:37.300
What was he even doing there?
Why didn't you tell us?

00:40:37.500 --> 00:40:39.500
He didn't want to go to a foster home.

00:40:39.800 --> 00:40:42.600
He didn't want to leave,
and I didn't want him to leave either.

00:40:42.900 --> 00:40:45.800
It's like, you force me to live
amongst these pod people...

00:40:46.100 --> 00:40:50.200
...and the first cool person I meet,
you kick him out of the house.

00:40:57.500 --> 00:41:00.000
I did the best I could.

00:41:00.200 --> 00:41:02.100
So did I.

00:41:08.400 --> 00:41:11.900
Come on. The police want to
ask us some more questions.

00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:14.900
Dispatch, is there a description...?

00:41:15.200 --> 00:41:16.700
Thank you.

00:41:21.800 --> 00:41:23.700
Just follow my lead.

00:41:29.200 --> 00:41:33.500
You and I need to talk.
And this time I want the truth.

00:42:04.200 --> 00:42:07.700
- I'm sorry.
- Ryan Atwood?

00:42:09.700 --> 00:42:12.000
We got some questions for you.

00:42:19.300 --> 00:42:22.800
- It was an accident.
- Yeah, you were there?

00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:30.200
Yeah.

00:42:30.400 --> 00:42:33.100
Then we got some questions
for you too.

00:42:36.500 --> 00:42:39.200
Officer, I'm Mr. Atwood's attorney.

00:42:39.500 --> 00:42:43.000
Please don't ask him any questions
unless I'm present.

00:42:43.700 --> 00:42:46.700
Ryan, keep your mouth shut.

00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:49.700
You too.
